# tests/mir_alias_facts_lane_test.tg — third-audit item 38 (and the
# per-call region slice of item 37): the convention-derived call alias/
# memory facts at MIR.
#
# The engine lives in tg_compiler/mir.tg (the CONVENTION-DERIVED CALL
# ALIAS/MEMORY FACTS section): mir_alias_facts_of_call derives a per-call
# MutationRegion from the typed access effects (let/inout/sink/set) plus
# the argument operand shape, and exposes call_may_read / call_may_write /
# call_is_barrier / call_consumes_root / call_initializes_root /
# call_root_is_exclusive. The same region drives the dead-store-
# elimination call classification and the pass-5 call-aware reverse sweep,
# and the access-fact forwarding terminator kill.
#
# The self-checking lane rows (mir_alias_facts_lane_check) build minimal
# MirFunctions BY HAND and assert:
#   A1 the audit's `def f(let a, inout b, sink c, set d)` call facts;
#   A2 DSE eliminating a store overwritten before a let-only call;
#   A3 the negative: an inout (read+write) call keeps the store;
#   A4 the aggregate (String) sink source's overwritten store is deleted;
#   A5 the pointer-argument barrier posture (conservative ALL);
#   A6 inout exclusivity through access-fact forwarding (a fact of an
#      unrelated local survives an inout call on another root).
#
# Run with the repo root as the working directory:
#   tg test tests/mir_alias_facts_lane_test.tg

use std::test::assert

use tg_compiler::mir::{mir_alias_facts_lane_check}

@test
def test_mir_alias_facts_lane() -> Unit
  let rows = mir_alias_facts_lane_check()
  assert(rows.len() == 0, "mir alias facts lane mismatches: " + rows.join("; "))
end
